    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2515e2e5-1042-5aeb-8a37-92801325ba00",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -8 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $D$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -8 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{4} :={R}_{4}+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{5} :={R}_{5}+\\left(\\frac{2}{7}\\right){R}_{4} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $D$ has $5$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $5.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
